1
00:03:06,486 --> 00:03:12,486
He is afraid. He is totally alone. He is 3,000,000 light years from home.

2
00:06:12,972 --> 00:06:18,972
E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial is a science fiction, adventure,
family film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:09:19,459 --> 00:09:25,459
An alien is left behind on Earth and saved by the 10-year-old
Elliott who decides to keep him hidden in his home.

4
00:12:25,945 --> 00:12:31,945
While a task force hunts for the extra-terrestrial, Elliott, his brother, and his little sister Gertie
form an emotional bond with their new friend, and try to help him find his way home.

5
00:15:32,432 --> 00:15:38,432
Elliott, played by Henry Thomas.

6
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:44,918
Gertie, played by Drew Barrymore.

7
00:21:45,405 --> 00:21:51,405
Michael, played by Robert MacNaughton.

8
00:24:51,891 --> 00:24:57,891
Keys, played by Peter Coyote.

9
00:27:58,378 --> 00:28:04,378
Mary, played by Dee Wallace.

10
00:31:04,864 --> 00:31:10,864
Pretty Girl, played by Erika Eleniak.

11
00:34:11,351 --> 00:34:17,351
the Extra-Terrestrial (or simply E.T.) is a 1982 American science fiction film
produced and directed by Steven Spielberg and written by Melissa Mathison.

12
00:37:17,837 --> 00:37:23,837
It tells the story of Elliott, a boy who befriends an
extraterrestrial that he names E.T.

13
00:40:24,324 --> 00:40:30,324
who has been stranded on Earth.

14
00:43:30,810 --> 00:43:36,810
Along with his friends and family, Elliott must find a way to help E.T.

15
00:46:37,297 --> 00:46:43,297
find his way home.

16
00:49:43,783 --> 00:49:49,783
The film stars Dee Wallace, Henry Thomas, Peter Coyote,
Robert MacNaughton, and Drew Barrymore.

17
00:52:50,270 --> 00:52:56,270
The film's concept was based on an imaginary friend that
Spielberg created after his parents' divorce.

18
00:55:56,756 --> 00:56:02,756
In 1980, Spielberg met Mathison and developed a new story
from the unrealized project Night Skies.

19
00:59:03,243 --> 00:59:09,243
In less than two months, Mathison wrote the first
draft of the script, titled E.T.

20
01:02:09,729 --> 01:02:15,729
and Me, which went through two rewrites.

21
01:05:16,216 --> 01:05:22,216
The project was rejected by Columbia Pictures, who
doubted its commercial potential.

22
01:08:22,702 --> 01:08:28,702
Universal Pictures eventually purchased the script for $1 million.

23
01:11:29,189 --> 01:11:35,189
Filming took place from September to December 1981 on a budget of $10.5 million.

24
01:14:35,675 --> 01:14:41,675
Unlike most films, E.T.

25
01:17:42,162 --> 01:17:48,162
was shot in rough chronological order to facilitate convincing
emotional performances from the young cast.

26
01:20:48,648 --> 01:20:54,648
The animatronics for the film were designed by Carlo Rambaldi.

27
01:23:55,135 --> 01:24:01,135
premiered as the closing film of the Cannes Film Festival on May 26,
1982, and was released in the United States on June 11.

28
01:27:01,621 --> 01:27:07,621
The film was a smash hit at the box office, surpassing Star Wars (1977) to become the highest-grossing film of all
time, a record it held for eleven years until Spielberg's own Jurassic Park surpassed it in 1993.

29
01:30:08,108 --> 01:30:14,108
received universal acclaim from critics, and is regarded as one of
the greatest and most influential films ever made.

30
01:33:14,594 --> 01:33:20,594
It received nine nominations at the 55th Academy Awards, winning Best Original Score, Best Visual Effects, Best
Sound, and Best Sound Editing in addition to being nominated for Best Picture and Best Director.

31
01:36:21,081 --> 01:36:27,081
It also won five Saturn Awards and two Golden Globe Awards.

32
01:39:27,567 --> 01:39:33,567
The film was re-released in 1985 and again in 2002 to celebrate its 20th
anniversary, with altered shots, visual effects, and additional scenes.

33
01:42:34,054 --> 01:42:40,054
It was also re-released in IMAX on August 12, 2022,
to celebrate its 40th anniversary.

34
01:45:40,540 --> 01:45:46,540
In 1994, the film was added to the United States National Film Registry of the Library of
Congress, who deemed it "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant."

35
01:48:47,027 --> 01:48:53,027
The film explores themes of farewell, space
marine, operation, flying saucer, nasa.

36
01:51:53,513 --> 01:51:59,513
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
